A small, cross-platform World of Warcraft addon manager

Usage:
  knapsack [flags]
  knapsack [command]

Available Commands:
  add         Add addons to the profile and install them
  check       Show what update would do, without changing anything
  completion  Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  config      Manage profiles and config.toml
  help        Help about any command
  info        Show details of one addon
  list        List the profile's addons and whether they're up to date
  remove      Uninstall addons and remove them from the profile
  self-update Update knapsack to the newest release
  sources     List addon sources and manage their API keys
  update      Upgrade outdated addons and install missing ones
  version     Print the knapsack version

Flags:
      --config string   use this config file instead of the default
  -v, --verbose         show progress and the underlying cause of errors

Use "knapsack [command] --help" for more information about a command.
